1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
<font color="#20e020">HI removed, cleaned
and corrected by Lunar Team</font>

2
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:45,461
Victim is Christine Tanner, 15.

3
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:47,755
Drowned. Washed up on the beach
in Santa Marta.

4
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:49,590
- Who's got the ultraviolet?
- Yup.

5
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,884
- She drowned. Why us?
- Coroner found a wound...

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,928
...consistent with getting hit in the head
with a surfboard...

7
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:57,431
...and water in her lungs,
only it was ditch water.

8
00:00:57,599 --> 00:01:00,142
- No salt, lot of bugs.
- So the killer is clever...

9
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,478
...but not as clever as he thinks he is.

10
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:04,480
Santa Marta sheriff's
not taking this?

11
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:06,148
State beach, state case.

12
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:09,485
All right, what are you doing?

13
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:13,989
Grace is mentally telling me
where she hid the van keys.

14
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:16,867
If I find them, I get to drive.

15
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,786
So now you're psychic.

16
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:21,163
Oh, no, no, no. This is all science.

17
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,957
Concentrate, Grace.

18
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,293
Tell me with your mind only.

19
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:30,756
Forward, backward, left, right.

20
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:33,467
- How is that science?
- Shh!

21
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:37,262
He watched you hide the keys.

22
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,807
From the men's room?
That would be a trick.

23
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:53,320
Hmm.

24
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:13,382
Who's got shotgun?

25
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,552
Can we go now?

26
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:29,690
Leah.

27
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,358
Go ahead.

28
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:59,636
- You had the keys the whole time.
- Let it go, man.

29
00:02:59,804 --> 00:03:02,347
- Did you have the keys?
- If I tell you how it's done...

30
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:05,517
...The Magic Circle will send
a team of assassins to kill us all.

31
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:06,727
It's the law.

32
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:08,604
Her body was discovered
on this beach.

33
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:12,900
That means she was put in the water
anywhere within a mile north of here.

34
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:15,611
Any further, current would have
taken her out to Mexico.

35
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:19,281
- How long was she in the water?
- Still waiting on the coroner's report.

36
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:31,460
Hey. Excuse me.

37
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:34,129
- Are you guys cops?
- CBI.

38
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:37,466
- What's CBI?
- California Bureau of Investigation.

39
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:38,800
Cops.

40
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:41,094
Cops.

41
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:43,055
So is it true what they're saying?

42
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:46,642
- Somebody killed Chris?
- Yes, it is true.

43
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:49,603
You were Christine's friend?

44
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:52,439
Yeah.

45
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,733
We hang at the same breaks.

46
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:56,652
I love Chris.

47
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,571
- What happened?
- We don't know yet.

48
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:02,282
- What's your name?
- Uh, Hope. That's Win.

49
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,659
- Hi.
- Hey.

50
00:04:03,826 --> 00:04:06,662
When was the last time
you saw Christine?

51
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,997
Uh, three days ago.

52
00:04:09,165 --> 00:04:11,667
Sunset patrol. Epic north-east swell.

53
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:15,420
Chris loved to go out at sunset.

54
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:18,382
She would stay out
till it was dark as dark.

55
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:21,510
How did she seem lately?
Just, you know, any enemies...

56
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,805
...or stuff like that?

57
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,515
Uh, not around here.

58
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,433
Everybody loved Chris.

59
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:30,519
- Was she dating anybody?
- Dating?

60
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:32,646
Okay, was she hooking up with anybody?

61
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,189
Danny Kurtik, mostly.

62
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:35,524
Jeez, Hope.

63
00:04:36,734 --> 00:04:38,527
What? They were hooking up.

64
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:42,030
Danny would never hurt Chris.

65
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:44,199
Duh. Of course not.

66
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,909
That's not what they were asking.

67
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:48,161
They were asking
who she was hooking up with.

68
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:52,124
Which would be Danny.
It wasn't a big dark secret.

69
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:55,544
I need you to write down your names
and numbers we can reach you at.

70
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,421
- Win?
- Yeah.

71
00:04:57,588 --> 00:04:59,548
If Chris was a color,
what color would she be?

72
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,509
Uh, orange or pink.

73
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:04,177
No, orange is right.

74
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,805
If she were an animal,
what kind of animal would she be?

75
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,724
Uh, I don't know.

76
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,726
A rabbit?

77
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:14,396
How's this relevant?

78
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:17,232
Everything's relevant.

79
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:22,237
Chris was good people.

80
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:23,739
I hope you find who did this.

81
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:26,408
We'll do our best.

82
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:31,413
- How is that relevant?
- We're looking for someone...

83
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:34,207
- ...who doesn't like orange rabbits.
- Exactly.

84
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:36,835
You know what, boys?
I like it here.

85
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,546
Yeah.

86
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:42,257
- I think I'll stay for a while.
- What?

87
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,595
Okay.

88
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:52,517
Let's just leave him here.

89
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:12,704
Excuse the mess.

90
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:15,165
Chrissy was the house-proud one
around here.

91
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,666
We understand.

92
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:19,294
- Mr. Tanner?
- Huh?

93
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:22,255
We may have to ask you
some tough questions, so...

94
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:28,220
That's okay.

95
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:31,473
Can't tell Lisa nothing
she hasn't heard before, and Micah don't...

96
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:33,475
He don't give a damn. He's slow.

97
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:37,145
He's just sad because he sees Lisa is.

98
00:06:37,313 --> 00:06:38,605
All the same.

99
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,859
- Come on, kids.
- Come on, Micah. Let's go.

100
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:47,489
- Can you take him outside?
- You got it, Dad.

101
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,991
Come on, let's go outside.

102
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:55,747
So when did you notice
Christine was missing?

103
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:58,625
Yesterday morning.
She hadn't made nothing for the kids.

104
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:01,670
I realized I hadn't seen her in a while.

105
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:04,673
I mean, she may be away one night
and I wouldn't know, but...

106
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:07,050
When was the last time you saw her?

107
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:08,552
Monday morning.

108
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:10,554
Any idea where she was
during that time?

109
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:14,307
No. No, Chrissy's real independent.
You never...

110
00:07:15,226 --> 00:07:16,977
Never had to worry about Chrissy.

111
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:20,188
Two days to notice your daughter's gone
and another to report it.

112
00:07:20,898 --> 00:07:22,023
I work.

113
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:24,901
I mean, I work construction.
I never miss a day.

114
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:27,362
I can't watch her all the time.

115
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,030
Her mother's not around?

116
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:32,159
She died. She was killed.

117
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:35,162
- In a car wreck.
- I'm sorry.

118
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:38,832
Almost five years ago now.

119
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,792
Drunk driver T-boned her.

120
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:43,712
College kid.

121
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:46,214
Walked away laughing.

122
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:48,758
Not a scratch. You know?

123
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:51,052
Not a scratch.

124
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:57,392
So Christine kind of took over
for her mom, huh?

125
00:07:58,478 --> 00:07:59,728
Cooked, cleaned.

126
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,981
- Looked after the little ones.
- Yeah.

127
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:05,400
Don't know what we're gonna do now.

128
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:07,402
Christine was arrested last year.

129
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:10,197
No, it was stupid.

130
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:12,115
It was a couple of joints.
No big deal.

131
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,409
Well, how is it she got into drugs?

132
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:16,661
She wasn't into drugs.
She was straight-edge.

133
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:20,081
- It's her dumbass friend, Darlene.
- Darlene.

134
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:22,125
- Last name?
- Pappas.

135
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:26,046
But Chrissy wasn't hanging out
much with Darlene anymore.

136
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:29,674
Not since she got into surfing
and started hanging with a different crowd.

137
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:31,426
- Who were they?
- Surfers, you know.

138
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:34,471
Not like bum surfers.
They just seem like good kids, you know.

139
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:35,931
They were upscale.

140
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:40,310
They'd pick her up in their
Audis and whatnot.

141
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:42,020
A good influence on Christine.

142
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:45,815
They helped her with her schoolwork
and she was thinking about college.

143
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:47,859
Anybody in particular she was close to?

144
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,611
I didn't really know them.

145
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:51,488
There's names I'd hear all the time.

146
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,532
There was, like,
Andy and Danny and Hope.

147
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:58,453
And then here was this new guy,
Flipper, she'd talk about lately.

148
00:08:58,621 --> 00:08:59,746
Talked about how?

149
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:02,582
Just that she was...
You know, they were hanging together.

150
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,626
You know, like, "I'll see you at Flipper's."

151
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:07,504
Hey, Lisa?

152
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,798
- Honey?
- Yeah, Dad?

153
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:13,301
Hey, honey, could you, uh,
fix some lunch for your brother please?

154
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:15,220
Yeah. Got it.

155
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:17,138
Thanks.

156
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:58,513
What, you didn't bring a bucket?

157
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:18,491
- Are you okay?
- Damn it.

158
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,871
- It's gotta be tough.
- What?

159
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:24,914
I mean, a drunk driver.

160
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,083
Isn't that what happened
to your mother?

161
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:30,879
Sorry. It's not my business.

162
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,632
We don't discuss
our personal lives in this unit.

163
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:37,177
It's not useful and it's not professional.

164
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,555
Cho.

165
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:43,183
Names to check. Darlene Pappas...

166
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,018
...Andy, Danny...

167
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:46,436
...Hope and Flipper.

168
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,688
Flipper? Okay.

169
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:50,774
Uh-huh.

170
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,734
Got it. Hold on.

171
00:10:57,448 --> 00:11:00,533
There's a Darlene Pappas in lock-up.
Possession, resisting arrest.

172
00:11:00,701 --> 00:11:03,203
- I'll get her in here.
- Great. Where's Jane?

173
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:05,288
Jane?

174
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:08,375
He's still pursuing inquiries
at the beach.

175
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:14,756
Good job.

176
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:44,202
Darlene, you're a friend
of Christine Tanner?

177
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:47,038
What do you want?

178
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:48,289
Christine's dead.

179
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:53,461
What do you want?

180
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:56,131
I want you to help us find out
who killed her.

181
00:11:56,298 --> 00:11:58,758
Killed? How?

182
00:11:58,926 --> 00:12:01,261
- Drowned.
- Drowned.

183
00:12:02,304 --> 00:12:03,346
Damn.

184
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:06,141
Who does she know
that might have reason to do this?

185
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:11,813
Well, now that you mention it...

186
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:12,981
...there was a guy.

187
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:15,650
What was his name?

188
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:20,488
Yes, Darlene.
If you help us, I'll talk to the prosecutor.

189
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:24,117
See if we can help you
with these charges you've got pending.

190
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:25,827
Okay.

191
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:31,040
Well, last year,
she was banging an older guy.

192
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,667
Like old.

193
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:35,503
- She called him Pops.
- No name? Just Pops?

194
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:37,589
Pops. That's it.

195
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:41,009
One time, uh,
she said he was getting weird.

196
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:44,304
She was talking about dumping him,
but I don't know if she ever did.

197
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:46,556
Like I say,
we haven't been tight for a while.

198
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:49,642
That's interesting,
but it's not enough for a call to the DA.

199
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:52,520
Did she say anything else about him?

200
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,355
Anything at all?

201
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,316
Uh...

202
00:12:56,525 --> 00:12:58,735
He was good in bed.

203
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:04,032
And he liked '50s music,
like Elvis and stuff.

204
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,533
I mean, that's it.

205
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:10,497
That's enough, right?

206
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:12,415
Well, call the DA.

207
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:16,377
Got a hit with those deputy interviews.

208
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:19,380
Philip Handler, goes by Flipper.
Badass surfer. Long sheet...

209
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:21,841
...including assault on a woman
a few years back.

210
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:23,718
- How bad?
- Hundred-stitches bad.

211
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,887
- Got an address.
- Let's go.

212
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:58,127
Philip Handler? Police.

213
00:13:58,295 --> 00:14:00,046
May we speak with you, please?

214
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:06,511
Mr. Handler?

215
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,887
Clear.

216
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,438
Mr. Handler?

217
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,774
Hey, these friends of yours?

218
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:23,111
Oh, hey, guys. Come in.

219
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:26,406
Come in. I'm just about to discredit
Nimzowitsch's theory...

220
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:29,075
...on the French advance
once and for all.

221
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:30,785
- Dream on, trick.
- Hmm.

222
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:36,624
Huh? Ha-ha-ha.

223
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,634
What led you to Flipper, anyway?

224
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:49,512
His hair. It's braided the exact same way
as the victim.

225
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,097
She did his 'do.

226
00:14:56,645 --> 00:14:59,814
I guess, uh, you must be bad cop.

227
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,649
I try.

228
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,484
Tough.

229
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:04,944
Go to it, sister.

230
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,780
You can be pretty tough yourself.

231
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:10,116
Roberta Varnushi.

232
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,160
- You did quite a number on her.
- Uh...

233
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:15,580
We had different expectations...

234
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:18,708
...that led to friction.

235
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:21,461
But, um, what can you do?

236
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:24,047
Friction. She nearly died.

237
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:28,176
Do you know what she was doing
that started the argument when I hit her?

238
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:33,681
She was pouring the sump oil from her car
right into the storm drain. Okay?

239
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:37,185
You might as well take an ax
and go chop up a family of dolphins.

240
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:41,397
Was Christine Tanner
damaging marine life somehow?

241
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:43,691
What? No.

242
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:46,694
Chris understood.

243
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:48,821
Chris was a child of the ocean.

244
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:51,074
You like hanging out with children,
don't you?

245
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:54,160
I do.

246
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:58,081
They're pure in flesh and spirit.

247
00:15:58,332 --> 00:16:00,041
What's not to like?

248
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:02,377
Christine was a beautiful girl.

249
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:04,712
Yes, she was.

250
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,757
So why'd you kill her?

251
00:16:11,261 --> 00:16:12,971
I didn't kill her.

252
00:16:13,138 --> 00:16:14,263
Why would I kill her?

253
00:16:14,431 --> 00:16:16,057
Did you have sex with her?

254
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:19,018
Oh, I thought about it.

255
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,853
I thought about it a lot.

256
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:22,438
But no, I didn't.

257
00:16:22,606 --> 00:16:23,856
- You know why?
- Why?

258
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:26,109
Because it would be wrong.

259
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:28,695
And I'm all about doing what's right.

260
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:31,406
I wait until they hit legal age.

261
00:16:31,573 --> 00:16:33,741
Then, bam.

262
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:36,703
Happy birthday, baby.

263
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:39,247
When was the last time you saw her?

264
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:42,583
Oh, so you can try and pin this on me?
No, thanks.

265
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:48,423
The thing is, Flip, Lisbon is looking at you
like you're a pork chop...

266
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:51,217
...because you fit the profile.
Your life is in chaos.

267
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,261
You're lonely, you're depressed...

268
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:55,596
...you're addicted to drugs
and pornography...

269
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:57,765
...and a little nuts, to be honest.

270
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:01,352
You're exactly the kind of man
that does terrible things to women.

271
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:10,820
Uh, but I don't think you did this.

272
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,574
Because I think, deep down,
you're a good man.

273
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:17,744
You should learn to use your bishops
a little more efficiently...

274
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:20,830
...but otherwise, a good man.

275
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,459
I saw Chris three days ago.

276
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:27,670
Sunset patrol at Devon Point break.

277
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:31,466
Was that Monday?
With Hope and Win and those guys?

278
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:34,594
Right. We rode until dark...

279
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:38,014
...and then we partied a while
on the beach.

280
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:42,351
And then I went home.

281
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,480
On my mother's life.

282
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:50,943
What do you mean, "person of interest"?

283
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:54,030
- This guy kill my Chrissy?
- Mr. Tanner, if we make an arrest...

284
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:56,491
...you'll be the first person I call,
I promise.

285
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,995
I'm gonna have somebody take you home.

286
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,040
This him?

287
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:05,958
Is this him?

288
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:09,337
Calm down. You need to go home,
take care of your children.

289
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:12,340
You're dead, bastard! You're dead!

290
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,509
You're dead, you bastard!

291
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,177
Go home, now!

292
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,138
Look at me.

293
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,516
Look at me.

294
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:25,394
Look at me. You need to go home.

295
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:31,859
Let's go home, Daddy.

296
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,825
Come on.

297
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:49,001
Lisbon.

298
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,174
Yeah.

299
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,970
Coroner told me Christine's body
was put in the water...

300
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:00,721
...sometime early Tuesday morning.

301
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:02,890
So that Monday-night party is critical.

302
00:19:03,058 --> 00:19:05,351
Somebody there had to have known
what happened.

303
00:19:05,519 --> 00:19:07,436
Okay, boss, we're on it.

304
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,657
Hi, people.

305
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:23,536
Thank you very much, ma'am,
but, uh, we don't need a grief councilor.

306
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:25,413
We know how to grieve.

307
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,540
Good,
because I'm not a grief councilor.

308
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:31,294
Principal didn't want to say "homicide
detective" in front of the students.

309
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:33,671
- Agent Lisbon, CBI.
- Hey, guys.

310
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,339
Hope and Win, I know.

311
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:38,885
You must be Danny and Andy.
Quick test:

312
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:41,596
If you could be any animal you want,
what would you be?

313
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:43,598
- Dolphin.
- You?

314
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:46,100
Uh, same. Or a killer whale.

315
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:47,852
A gull. No, a hawk.

316
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:51,355
Uh, uh, a tiger.

317
00:19:51,523 --> 00:19:53,107
Interesting.

318
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,609
Why?

319
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:57,069
When we spoke about Monday night
at Devon Point...

320
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,739
...you didn't mention
you had a party after surfing.

321
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:02,742
A party? No, it wasn't a party.

322
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,869
Not what Flipper says.

323
00:20:05,495 --> 00:20:07,622
Flipper told? Dude.

324
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:10,124
Come on, guys. I mean, we partied.

325
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:12,668
Threw a little Frisbee.
What's the big deal?

326
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:14,712
No big deal.
You were the last people...

327
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,131
...aside from her killer
to see Christine alive.

328
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,008
She was drowned later that night.

329
00:20:19,176 --> 00:20:20,635
- That night?
- Are you serious?

330
00:20:20,802 --> 00:20:21,844
Oh, my God.

331
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:27,600
Um, sorry, we have to go.
We have AP English.

332
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:29,185
We'll walk you.

333
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:33,856
Tell us about this party Monday night.

334
00:20:34,024 --> 00:20:36,108
You didn't say anything about it before.
Why?

335
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,693
And don't lie or I'll know.

336
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:39,862
We were drinking beer, ma'am.

337
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,364
- Shut up.
- What.

338
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,616
We're all gonna be applying
for college soon.

339
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:46,702
- We can't get caught for drinking.
- My mom would exterminate me.

340
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:48,329
Plus we were trespassing.

341
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:52,625
The, uh, beach at Devon Point
is totally a private property.

342
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:55,628
Danny, what does Devon Point
mean to you?

343
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:59,590
Uh, it's my Dad's land.

344
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:02,260
And, uh, he's building
these heinous condos.

345
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:04,679
We go there to spite him, I guess.

346
00:21:04,846 --> 00:21:07,473
- Who else was there that night?
- Us and Flipper.

347
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:09,016
It wasn't exactly raging.

348
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:12,311
We all cut out about 10, 10:30 maybe.

349
00:21:12,479 --> 00:21:15,856
Chris stayed to clean up.
She's all, uh, "save our oceans," you know?

350
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:18,401
- Did Flipper leave then too?
- He cut out early.

351
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:20,278
After we ran out of brews.

352
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:22,238
Do you think he came back maybe?

353
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:24,198
Like Flipper did it? No.

354
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:27,702
- We shouldn't have left her there, guys.
- She wanted to stay.

355
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:29,870
- Ask me, she was meeting someone.
- Shut up.

356
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:33,874
- You don't know that.
- No, but I think it and so do you.

357
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:36,627
Danny asked her to go home with him.
She said no.

358
00:21:38,171 --> 00:21:39,839
You and Chris were lovers?

359
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:41,674
Lovers?

360
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:44,510
Uh, no. We hooked up on occasion.

361
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:46,178
You made love. You were lovers.

362
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:49,056
No. Uh, I mean,
Andy was totally there too.

363
00:21:49,224 --> 00:21:51,017
- Right, Andy?
- Yeah.

364
00:21:51,601 --> 00:21:54,186
It wasn't a big deal.
We're all just friends.

365
00:21:54,354 --> 00:21:56,105
Andy and I hook up with
Hope sometimes.

366
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:58,399
Doesn't mean we're lovers.

367
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:01,736
Yeah. That would be weird.

368
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,405
Yeah, I guess.

369
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:07,533
You ever hear of anyone named Pops?

370
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:11,704
- Pops?
- Yeah.

371
00:22:12,372 --> 00:22:13,831
Uh, no.

372
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:17,126
Okay. Well, that's all we need for now.
Thank you.

373
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:18,961
- Thank you.
- Thanks, bye.

374
00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:21,088
Don't leave town.

375
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:23,090
Now, that's a cop joke.

376
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:33,642
How long you gonna be, you think?

377
00:22:33,810 --> 00:22:36,687
Mr. Rayburn, Christine Tanner's murder
may have occurred here.

378
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:38,272
It takes as long as it takes.

379
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,399
I got the developer way up my tailpipe.

380
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:43,486
Three weeks behind,
thanks to the crappy labor pool here.

381
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:46,072
Economy like this
and people don't show up for work?

382
00:22:46,239 --> 00:22:48,449
- Boggles my mind.
- Anybody not show up lately?

383
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:52,119
Night guard, just this week.
Walked off the job.

384
00:22:52,287 --> 00:22:55,790
Cement truck shows up in the morning,
can't get on the freaking site.

385
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:57,625
That alone put me back six hours.

386
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,627
- When'd he quit?
- Monday.

387
00:22:59,795 --> 00:23:03,047
- What section you working then?
- Southeast quad.

388
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:04,924
What's his name, the night guard?

389
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:06,425
Eddie Garcia.

390
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:09,261
I got his paperwork in the site office,
if you want it.

391
00:23:09,429 --> 00:23:11,514
Jorge, what, are you nuts?

392
00:23:11,681 --> 00:23:13,307
That load goes over here.

393
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:25,820
The paperwork?

394
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:27,822
Right.

395
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:30,157
What, you think he might have, uh,
done this murder?

396
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:31,784
Lisbon!

397
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,119
Come take a look at this.

398
00:23:36,123 --> 00:23:37,164
What?

399
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:43,671
Oh, yeah.

400
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:47,341
Mr. Rayburn!

401
00:23:53,390 --> 00:23:54,765
See that?

402
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,685
- What is it?
- Tip of Eddie Garcia's nose.

403
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:00,521
Get out of here.

404
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,441
Oh!

405
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:17,246
How is it you don't even notice
a nose in your floor?

406
00:24:17,414 --> 00:24:20,708
It's what I'm telling you.
We're trying to finish this thing too fast.

407
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:23,878
What the hell's going on?

408
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:27,882
Oh, for heaven's sakes.

409
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:29,884
Is that a person? Someone I employ?

410
00:24:30,051 --> 00:24:31,218
We think so.

411
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:34,388
God, help me. If it's not one thing, it's...

412
00:24:34,556 --> 00:24:35,931
Mr. Kurtik?

413
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,516
Dane Kurtik?

414
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:39,560
OSHA, right? Just talk to my lawyers.

415
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:42,563
As you saw, I have no knowledge
of this regrettable incident.

416
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:44,607
CBI. Serious Crimes Unit.

417
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:47,735
Serious Crimes?
The man fell into wet cement.

418
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:51,322
Someone had been here with a camera,
he'd be on America's Funniest Videos.

419
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:52,698
Serious Crimes. Come on.

420
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:54,867
I'm sorry, sir. This is now a crime scene.

421
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:57,870
You have to suspend work
until we're done investigating.

422
00:24:58,038 --> 00:25:00,206
Suspend work? Hell.

423
00:25:00,373 --> 00:25:02,541
I'm calling Tommy Alvarez,
the sheriff.

424
00:25:02,709 --> 00:25:06,170
We believe this situation is related
to the death of Christine Tanner.

425
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:08,464
- You know her?
- I've heard the name, obviously.

426
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:09,715
It's been on the news.

427
00:25:09,883 --> 00:25:12,968
Your son Danny and Christine were close.
You never met her?

428
00:25:13,136 --> 00:25:15,221
Maybe I have.
My son has a lot of friends.

429
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:17,973
- Is this an interrogation? Is it?
- No, sir, it isn't.

430
00:25:18,141 --> 00:25:20,935
We appreciate your cooperation.
We'll be in touch, maybe.

431
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:22,770
Thank you.

432
00:25:25,857 --> 00:25:27,191
Hey, Pops.

433
00:25:32,656 --> 00:25:34,782
Hear you're good in bed.
What's the secret?

434
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:36,909
I don't know
what you're talking about.

435
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:40,538
But you mean to be offensive, I guess,
and you've succeeded very well.

436
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:42,748
I'll be taking this up with your superiors.

437
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:44,959
- What is your name?
- My name is Patrick Jane.

438
00:25:45,126 --> 00:25:47,169
- Jane, stop.
- And I have no superiors.

439
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:50,089
I'll tell you what I'm talking about,
you sweaty pervert.

440
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:52,925
- Jane.
- You were having sex with a 15-year-old.

441
00:25:53,093 --> 00:25:54,134
Jane, stop.

442
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:55,844
- I never touched Christine.
- Liar.

443
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:58,973
And believe me when I tell you...

444
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:03,519
...that you just now made the worst mistake
of your miserable little life.

445
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:05,896
Believe me,
no matter how this turns out...

446
00:26:06,064 --> 00:26:07,565
...I've made worse mistakes.

447
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:10,609
You're lying about Christine.
You were laying her like carpet.

448
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,736
Arrest him, Lisbon. Statutory rape.

449
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:13,946
With what evidence?

450
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:16,490
He's playing rockabilly.

451
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:19,118
Fifties music. What more do you want?

452
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:23,038
I can only apologize
for my colleague's bizarre behavior.

453
00:26:23,206 --> 00:26:24,540
- I'm sorry.
- Lisbon, hush.

454
00:26:24,708 --> 00:26:26,000
Don't be so damn blinkered.

455
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:27,710
Look at him. He was raping her.

456
00:26:27,877 --> 00:26:30,004
I don't know yet
whether he killed her as well.

457
00:26:30,171 --> 00:26:31,505
Did you kill her?

458
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:33,674
Look me in the eye
and tell me the truth...

459
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:35,134
...filthy old goat.

460
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:39,096
- You don't talk...!
- Oh, aw.

461
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:41,849
How dare you?!

462
00:26:42,183 --> 00:26:44,018
Oh, oh.

463
00:26:46,062 --> 00:26:48,522
You brought him all the way back here,
why?

464
00:26:48,690 --> 00:26:51,233
The local sheriff begged me
not to put him in his jail.

465
00:26:51,401 --> 00:26:53,944
- Kurtik's a big cheese down there.
- That is a signal.

466
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:56,655
Is that not a signal
that we should cut this man loose?

467
00:26:56,823 --> 00:27:00,034
He hit Jane pretty good. People
were watching. I had to arrest him.

468
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:03,370
This guy is connected. This guy is...

469
00:27:04,706 --> 00:27:06,498
He has the governor's home number.

470
00:27:06,666 --> 00:27:09,585
And we both know
that Jane was asking for it.

471
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:13,839
You couldn't just give Kurtik
a stern talking-to instead?

472
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:15,549
What about Christine Tanner, sir?

473
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:18,719
If Kurtik was having sex with her,
that gives him motive to kill.

474
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:22,389
If. And that's a hunch.
Based on rockabilly.

475
00:27:22,557 --> 00:27:25,893
It's a Jane hunch.
You keep him around for a reason.

476
00:27:26,061 --> 00:27:29,313
Look, just let us work Kurtik
until his lawyer gets here.

477
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:33,192
- Maybe we can get something more.
- All right. Work him gently.

478
00:27:34,694 --> 00:27:36,779
Have a thing for youngsters
in general, Dane?

479
00:27:36,946 --> 00:27:39,657
Or was it Christine in particular
that appealed to you?

480
00:27:40,617 --> 00:27:43,994
That I can understand, because, you know,
you meet some 15-year-olds...

481
00:27:44,162 --> 00:27:47,164
...they're just as smart and mature
and articulate as any adult.

482
00:27:47,332 --> 00:27:48,916
Right?

483
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:52,586
They are adults, basically.
Maybe Christine was one of them.

484
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:56,090
Are you serious?

485
00:27:56,591 --> 00:27:59,593
Do you actually obtain confessions
with that gambit?

486
00:28:00,220 --> 00:28:02,179
- All the time.
- Amazing.

487
00:28:02,347 --> 00:28:03,806
People are stupid.

488
00:28:03,973 --> 00:28:05,432
Listen, I admire cops.

489
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:08,852
I think you do a great job.
I'm happy to sit here and chat with you...

490
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:10,437
...until my lawyer gets here.

491
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:14,817
But I'm not gonna say anything
you want to hear.

492
00:28:14,984 --> 00:28:17,111
- So relax, huh?
- He's not.

493
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:19,029
Is he?

494
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:21,281
He's not gonna confess.

495
00:28:21,449 --> 00:28:24,493
What'd you think, he'd break
under the bad lighting conditions?

496
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:26,995
- Let's go back to Devon Point.
- What for?

497
00:28:27,163 --> 00:28:30,541
So I can put the second half
of my cunning plan into effect.

498
00:28:31,209 --> 00:28:32,501
Jane, wait.

499
00:28:32,669 --> 00:28:34,503
What cunning plan?

500
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:36,672
Danny, hi. Patrick Jane.

501
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:38,340
Listen, we need your help.

502
00:28:38,508 --> 00:28:40,926
Do you want to help us catch
Christine's killer?

503
00:28:42,178 --> 00:28:43,971
Okay, then. Good.

504
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:47,641
Meet me at Devon Point
with your friends in, uh...

505
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:50,310
...two hours. Great.

506
00:28:50,478 --> 00:28:52,354
What cunning plan?

507
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:59,153
Just so you know, I'm suing the CBI
and the Attorney General's Office...

508
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:01,822
...for wrongful arrest
and unlawful imprisonment.

509
00:29:01,990 --> 00:29:05,534
And I will drop the suit
when they fire you and Agent Lisbon.

510
00:29:05,994 --> 00:29:06,994
Best of luck.

511
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,662
You're not scared of me, huh?

512
00:29:09,831 --> 00:29:12,499
It's a mistake. Heh.

513
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:17,004
Keep walking, Mr. Kurtik,
or I'm gonna have to arrest you again.

514
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,883
If you were 15 years younger...

515
00:29:21,050 --> 00:29:23,051
...I might give you a shot.

516
00:29:32,896 --> 00:29:34,354
- You guys see him?
- Mr. Jane?

517
00:29:34,522 --> 00:29:35,814
I don't see him.

518
00:29:36,691 --> 00:29:38,192
Mr. Jane?

519
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:40,819
Thanks for coming.

520
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:43,530
The police need your help.

521
00:29:43,698 --> 00:29:45,032
First Christine.

522
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,201
Then the security guard.
They're at a loss.

523
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:50,287
Did the guard stumble across
Chris being killed?

524
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:53,040
Maybe it was some kind of love triangle.

525
00:29:54,626 --> 00:29:58,170
Tell me, do you sincerely wanna help
catch Christine's murderer?

526
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:00,339
Even if the killer is someone
close to you?

527
00:30:00,507 --> 00:30:02,257
- Yes, of course.
- Of course, we would.

528
00:30:05,136 --> 00:30:07,346
Flipper served time
for assaulting a woman.

529
00:30:07,514 --> 00:30:09,640
- Did you know that?
- It was Flipper?

530
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:11,767
- He did it?
- Could be.

531
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:15,896
Then again, Danny...

532
00:30:17,065 --> 00:30:19,900
- ...Christine and your father had an affair.
- Wait. What?

533
00:30:20,068 --> 00:30:21,735
- Yeah.
- No way.

534
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:23,570
No, no, that's ridiculous.

535
00:30:23,738 --> 00:30:25,656
- No.
- Danny, get real.

536
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:27,908
We knew. We all knew.

537
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:34,289
Well, what'd you expect me to do,
turn in my own dad?

538
00:30:38,169 --> 00:30:41,839
I mean, it's not like
he forced Chris to do it, you know.

539
00:30:42,006 --> 00:30:44,758
She was into it.

540
00:30:46,427 --> 00:30:49,054
Was it your father she was going
to meet with that night?

541
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:50,973
- Yes.
- No.

542
00:30:53,059 --> 00:30:54,560
Well, I don't know.

543
00:30:56,855 --> 00:31:00,566
Just because they're having an affair
doesn't mean your father killed Christine.

544
00:31:01,442 --> 00:31:03,902
- It could have been Flipper.
- Right.

545
00:31:04,070 --> 00:31:05,112
Or someone else.

546
00:31:06,406 --> 00:31:08,574
Didn't you say you had a way
of finding out?

547
00:31:13,246 --> 00:31:15,956
Actually, a way you can find out.

548
00:31:33,933 --> 00:31:38,270
I want to hypnotize you all so that
you can remember details of that night.

549
00:31:38,438 --> 00:31:40,147
It's safe. I'm fully trained.

550
00:31:40,315 --> 00:31:43,817
- I used to hypnotize people for a living.
- Uh, no, no, thanks.

551
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:47,529
Your subconscious minds may recall
things that could help us find the killer.

552
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:50,991
Hypnosis will let you
come up with those things.

553
00:31:51,159 --> 00:31:53,327
- Well, what kind of things?
- Who knows?

554
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,370
Maybe something Chris said.

555
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:58,582
Maybe a glimpse of someone
on the bluff there.

556
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:02,836
The smallest detail that you can recall
could be a vital clue.

557
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,364
I don't want you messing around
in my head, man. No offense.

558
00:32:05,506 --> 00:32:08,175
Ah, but that's the thing with hypnosis.

559
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:11,637
I can't mesmerize you against your will.
It's not possible.

560
00:32:11,804 --> 00:32:14,514
You are in control the whole time.

561
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:18,226
What do you say?

562
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:25,817
Good.

563
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:32,199
I want you to close your eyes...

564
00:32:33,493 --> 00:32:34,576
...and listen.

565
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:41,041
Listen only to my voice.

566
00:32:42,126 --> 00:32:43,752
Think.

567
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:45,879
Think back to that night.

568
00:32:47,715 --> 00:32:49,549
The bonfire.

569
00:32:50,385 --> 00:32:52,052
The sound of the ocean.

570
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:56,682
The sound of the ocean.

571
00:32:58,601 --> 00:33:01,019
I don't know what
you will recall of that night...

572
00:33:01,187 --> 00:33:03,397
...but I know that you will
recall something...

573
00:33:03,564 --> 00:33:06,900
...because it's all there in your memory.

574
00:33:10,363 --> 00:33:13,782
All you have to do is go back...

575
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:18,203
...back to that night and be there.

576
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:20,414
And there you are.

577
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:24,751
What is it, Hope? What do you see?

578
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:26,420
I see Danny's father.

579
00:33:26,587 --> 00:33:27,796
There, above the rocks.

580
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:30,674
- No, you don't.
- Shh.

581
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:31,925
What is he doing?

582
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:35,470
Staring at us.

583
00:33:36,389 --> 00:33:37,723
At Chris.

584
00:33:37,890 --> 00:33:40,267
That's it. Staring.

585
00:33:40,643 --> 00:33:41,935
What's wrong with him?

586
00:33:44,939 --> 00:33:46,481
Come back, Hope.

587
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:49,901
- What happened?
- You're okay.

588
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:52,070
You did very well, thank you.

589
00:33:52,238 --> 00:33:54,740
You really saw Mr. Kurtik?

590
00:33:54,907 --> 00:33:56,491
No, you didn't.

591
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:58,076
- You didn't.
- Danny, I'm sorry.

592
00:33:58,244 --> 00:33:59,619
I can't help what I saw.

593
00:34:00,747 --> 00:34:02,247
My dad didn't kill Christine.

594
00:34:02,415 --> 00:34:03,832
How do you know he didn't?

595
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,500
Yeah, how do you know?

596
00:34:08,588 --> 00:34:11,798
You know what,
screw all of you guys, okay?

597
00:34:13,676 --> 00:34:14,760
You guys suck.

598
00:34:14,927 --> 00:34:16,762
Danny, wait. Don't be mad.

599
00:34:16,929 --> 00:34:18,346
Danny, wait.

600
00:34:18,514 --> 00:34:20,766
Danny. Come on, stop.

601
00:34:21,517 --> 00:34:24,436
Danny's mad. We should go.

602
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:25,645
Screw Danny.

603
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:29,775
His dad killed Christine.

604
00:34:31,819 --> 00:34:33,487
Yeah.

605
00:34:34,155 --> 00:34:35,280
It's late anyway.

606
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:37,699
- Thanks for your help, guys.
- No problemo.

607
00:34:50,421 --> 00:34:52,255
So, what do you think? Did it work?

608
00:34:52,423 --> 00:34:54,174
I think.

609
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:58,970
Three, two, one, now.

610
00:35:03,184 --> 00:35:05,685
How cool would it have been
if one had walked in then?

611
00:35:06,437 --> 00:35:07,521
Hi.

612
00:35:10,566 --> 00:35:13,360
Did you arrest him? Did he confess?

613
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:15,904
Mr. Kurtik? No.

614
00:35:16,072 --> 00:35:19,866
Thing is, Hope, Mr. Kurtik
has a cast-iron alibi for that evening.

615
00:35:20,034 --> 00:35:23,203
So you couldn't have seen him
standing there on that bluff.

616
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:25,747
But that's so weird.

617
00:35:25,915 --> 00:35:28,667
In my trance, I saw him clear as day.

618
00:35:29,877 --> 00:35:32,504
- Maybe it's symbolic.
- You want symbolic?

619
00:35:32,672 --> 00:35:35,715
You're a hawk
and Christine was a rabbit.

620
00:35:38,386 --> 00:35:39,553
What does that even mean?

621
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,429
Bird of prey, rabbit.

622
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,306
You tell me.

623
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:46,393
What it means is
you never liked Christine Tanner.

624
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:47,894
Not true.

625
00:35:48,062 --> 00:35:51,022
What it means is
I never really hypnotized you.

626
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:54,860
You pretended to be in a trance
to give us a fake story...

627
00:35:55,027 --> 00:35:56,945
...and incriminate an innocent man.

628
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:59,114
No.

629
00:36:00,908 --> 00:36:02,909
No.

630
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,913
Just tell us what happened that night.

631
00:36:07,081 --> 00:36:08,456
From the beginning.

632
00:36:09,917 --> 00:36:11,793
Flipper already left...

633
00:36:11,961 --> 00:36:14,254
...wasted as usual.

634
00:36:27,351 --> 00:36:29,603
The guard told us to get out...

635
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:31,396
...or he'd call the cops.

636
00:36:31,564 --> 00:36:34,274
Danny told him to step off,
his dad owns the place.

637
00:36:35,401 --> 00:36:36,443
Hey!

638
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:38,236
Oh, my God.

639
00:36:45,786 --> 00:36:47,329
He's dead.

640
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:52,876
He didn't mean to. It was an accident.

641
00:36:53,502 --> 00:36:55,462
We couldn't help the guard, see?

642
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:57,005
But Danny, we could.

643
00:36:57,173 --> 00:36:59,799
So we all promised not to tell.

644
00:37:00,384 --> 00:37:01,676
All of us.

645
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:04,888
Except Chris.

646
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:06,514
Not Chris.

647
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:08,600
You gotta understand.

648
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:11,186
Everything Danny had worked for
his whole life...

649
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:15,190
...was just washing away,
because Chris has to do the right thing.

650
00:37:20,321 --> 00:37:22,155
He just hit her on the head.

651
00:37:22,740 --> 00:37:25,075
And then she was still moving...

652
00:37:25,243 --> 00:37:27,327
...so he dragged her to the trough there...

653
00:37:28,663 --> 00:37:30,747
...and drowned her in it.

654
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:33,500
Held her under until she stopped moving.

655
00:37:34,710 --> 00:37:37,587
And you, Win, and Andy
didn't say a word.

656
00:37:37,755 --> 00:37:39,172
Two people, murdered.

657
00:37:40,466 --> 00:37:42,342
What if I was next?

658
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:45,887
I've never seen Danny like that.

659
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:49,015
He was like a different person
or something.

660
00:37:49,183 --> 00:37:50,225
Okay, you're safe now.

661
00:37:54,272 --> 00:37:55,355
Excuse us.

662
00:38:10,162 --> 00:38:11,204
Hey.

663
00:38:11,372 --> 00:38:14,374
I can't let my dad be punished
for something he didn't do...

664
00:38:14,542 --> 00:38:16,084
...no matter what a tool he is.

665
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:17,669
- So you're confessing.
- Huh?

666
00:38:17,837 --> 00:38:19,212
Hmm?

667
00:38:19,380 --> 00:38:21,589
We know it was you
that killed Christine and the guard.

668
00:38:21,757 --> 00:38:22,882
What?

669
00:38:23,050 --> 00:38:26,094
No, no, no, that's not right.
Who told you that?

670
00:38:26,762 --> 00:38:29,723
It's so completely not true
that it's insane.

671
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:31,850
How can you do this?

672
00:38:32,018 --> 00:38:34,102
I knew you had a cold streak,
but this?

673
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:37,063
Danny, I'm sorry. I had to tell the truth.

674
00:38:37,231 --> 00:38:41,067
You're only making it worse by lying.
You're only deceiving yourself.

675
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:48,450
It was her, okay?

676
00:38:48,617 --> 00:38:50,452
It was her who killed Chris.

677
00:38:51,329 --> 00:38:54,497
Hope was jealous of her
ever since she started hanging out with us.

678
00:38:54,665 --> 00:38:57,167
Used to be Hope who was all that.

679
00:38:57,335 --> 00:38:58,501
Then Chris came along...

680
00:38:58,669 --> 00:39:01,963
...and we only hooked up with Hope
when Chris wasn't around.

681
00:39:02,131 --> 00:39:04,758
- That's so distorted and not true.
- No.

682
00:39:04,925 --> 00:39:06,968
I am telling the truth now.

683
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:11,431
The security guard...

684
00:39:13,601 --> 00:39:14,768
...it was an accident.

685
00:39:14,935 --> 00:39:17,062
Then Chris said
she was gonna call the police.

686
00:39:17,229 --> 00:39:20,732
She said we couldn't cover it up,
because it would be wrong.

687
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:21,941
Then Hope...

688
00:39:23,235 --> 00:39:25,945
I don't even know.
Hope just went crazy.

689
00:39:27,656 --> 00:39:29,324
Hit her.

690
00:39:29,909 --> 00:39:32,786
- She hit her!
- I did it for you, jerk!

691
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:34,788
I did it for you.

692
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:39,000
She was doing his dad.

693
00:39:39,168 --> 00:39:42,128
She's acting as a judge over his life...

694
00:39:42,296 --> 00:39:43,922
...telling him his life is over...

695
00:39:44,090 --> 00:39:48,676
...that he's going to jail because
she's gotta show integrity and morals?

696
00:39:50,554 --> 00:39:53,640
She was a prissy, hypocritical bitch.

697
00:39:53,808 --> 00:39:56,434
And she was gonna ruin his life.

698
00:40:08,864 --> 00:40:10,490
Hmm.

699
00:40:13,160 --> 00:40:14,452
It was Flipper.

700
00:40:14,620 --> 00:40:17,122
- Really?
- Yeah, it was Flipper.

701
00:40:17,289 --> 00:40:20,333
What if I said it was you, Andy?
You killed Christine.

702
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:22,460
What? That's bull.

703
00:40:22,628 --> 00:40:24,796
That's ridiculous.

704
00:40:30,678 --> 00:40:31,678
Have a seat.

705
00:40:35,182 --> 00:40:36,307
Don't be shy.

706
00:40:38,894 --> 00:40:40,854
I didn't kill her, man.

707
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:43,148
Sure, you did.

708
00:40:44,984 --> 00:40:46,025
And so did you.

709
00:40:47,570 --> 00:40:49,154
And you.

710
00:40:49,822 --> 00:40:51,531
And you.

711
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:53,533
All four of you killed her.

712
00:40:54,201 --> 00:40:57,537
Hope was always smarter
than any of you.

713
00:40:58,539 --> 00:41:00,248
You never appreciated that.

714
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:14,888
She made all of you take part
to make all of you equally guilty...

715
00:41:15,055 --> 00:41:17,599
...so that no one would tell
on the others.

716
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:21,895
And now you're all equally under arrest.

717
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:24,272
You have the right to remain silent.

718
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:27,859
Anything you say can and will be used
against you in a court of law.

719
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:30,778
You have the right to an attorney.
If you cannot...

720
00:41:34,992 --> 00:41:37,202
Statutory rape, huh?

721
00:41:38,412 --> 00:41:40,705
- What'll he get?
- He probably won't serve time.

722
00:41:40,873 --> 00:41:43,249
Not without Christine's testimony.

723
00:41:43,417 --> 00:41:45,752
But we'll have fun trying.

724
00:41:50,007 --> 00:41:51,591
You have good kids.

725
00:41:53,427 --> 00:41:54,969
Yeah, I do.

726
00:41:56,597 --> 00:41:58,431
You're all they have.

727
00:41:59,934 --> 00:42:02,268
Yeah, I know.

728
00:42:03,812 --> 00:42:05,730
Be good to them.

729
00:42:09,068 --> 00:42:10,318
I am good to them.

730
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:15,114
My father was a good man,
just like you are.

731
00:42:15,699 --> 00:42:16,950
And after my mother died...

732
00:42:17,117 --> 00:42:20,620
...he was a self-pitying drunk,
just like you are.

733
00:42:20,788 --> 00:42:22,288
He killed himself.

734
00:42:22,456 --> 00:42:24,624
Damn near killed me
and my brothers too.

735
00:42:26,835 --> 00:42:28,127
Get some help.

736
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:29,921
Your kids deserve it.

737
00:42:30,422 --> 00:42:31,631
So do you.

